WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.860
Anthropics new hardware standard gives ai agents a unified way to control lab equipment, boards, and cameras through one interface. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 155. Anthropic opened a research preview of its model hardware standard today. The effort invites partners in science, robotics, and manufacturing to shape a common driver layer for physical devices. It starts with lab and manufacturing gear, and will extend through Claude code to boards

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:58.640
and cameras under one interface. The preview will also generate new safety evaluations since current models still lack physical intuition from text and image training alone. Collaboration began with hhmi, and now seeks input across multiple industries before any open source release. This moves the agent tooling conversation forward from yesterday, because it targets the exact standardization gap that has limited reliable hardware control so far.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:26.160
OpenAI ran a randomized study with more than 1,000 students on a real university assignment. Students who combined chat GPT use with explicit, critical thinking training produced stronger answers and broader thinking than either approach alone. The study measured gains in originaled metrics and overall assignment scores. Builders working on educational agents should test similar training scaffolds before deploying raw model access.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:50.440
Cisco rolled out a single custom AI agent across its entire 90,000 person workforce. The deployment gives every worker the same agent tooling rather than scattered point solutions. Early results tie the rollout to measurable productivity lifts inside the company. The agent was built internally and distributed uniformly with attention to access controls and audit logging at this scale.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:02:10.940
AWS released guidance for combining Amazon quick with the fall platform to create agent driven creative pipelines. The setup lets agents orchestrate image and video generation steps with explicit tool calls. Developers can follow the published notebook to wire agents directly to fall endpoints without custom orchestration code.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:29.440
The pattern supports step-by-step agent control over generation parameters and output handling when reproducible pipelines matter. The PiEvo FE library version 0.30 uses genetic programming to discover and chain feature transformations for tabular data sets.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:46.360
It ships with more than 40 built-in transformers. Polars backed vectorized execution and multi-fidelity screening. The package is 100% scikit-learn compatible and includes an interactive HTML replay viewer for inspecting the evolutionary process.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:58.000
Higher-archical chaining allows evolved features to serve as build-in blocks for later generations and it supports island model parallel search plus post-search caruana ensembling.

